      "finalMessage": "Done. Porto Notes is built and shipped to `dist/`.\n\n## What's there\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `index.html` | Static shell — form, search, feed, plus a CSP meta tag |\n| `src/main.ts` | Wiring: state, render, form submit, search, fragment sync |\n| `src/richtext.ts` | Tokenizer + DOM builder for the inline tag set; `plainText` for search |\n| `src/url.ts` | Scheme vetting for link hrefs and avatar srcs |\n| `src/store.ts` | localStorage load/save, fixture seeding, id sequence, newest-first sort |\n| `src/hash.ts` | `#q=…&note=…` parse/format |\n| `src/style.css` | Styles (external file, so no `'unsafe-inline'` needed) |\n\n## Verification\n\n`pnpm smoke` passes (build + headless load, zero console errors). I also drove the built app through the full element contract in a headless browser — 35/35 checks: seeding and newest-first order, bold/italic/link/`<br>` rendering, avatar-only-when-given, case-insensitive filtering on title and body, the exact `results for \"…\"` text, `aria-current` on selection, `#q=…&note=…` round-tripping through reload, form clearing, id continuation (7, 8), and persistence. That script was temporary and is deleted; `dist/` is the current build.\n\n## Two judgment calls worth your attention\n\n**The `#q=port&note=3` example is self-contradictory against `fixtures.json`** — `port` matches only note 1, so note 3 is filtered out of the feed. I implemented the feed as *strictly* filtered and kept the selection alive in state and in the fragment: loading that URL shows one note, keeps `#q=port&note=3` intact, and clearing the search makes note 3 reappear with `aria-current=\"true\"`. So a test asserting \"note 3 is visible and selected at that exact URL\" would fail, while \"type a query, count the notes\" assertions stay correct. If the shared suite expects the selected note pinned into a filtered feed, that's a one-line change in `visibleNotes()`.\n\n**Rich text is rendered by an allow-list tokenizer that builds DOM nodes — the app never touches `innerHTML`.** Only `<b> <strong> <i> <em> <a href> <br>` become elements; everything else, including `<img onerror=…>` and `<script>`, stays a text node and displays literally. Link hrefs and avatar URLs are scheme-checked (`javascript:` and `data:text/html` dropped; `data:image/*` kept, since the fixtures need it and SVG in an `<img>` can't execute). Search matches the rendered text rather than the raw markup, so searching `b` doesn't hit every bold note.\n\nMinor notes: I dropped the usual skip link because a `#feed` href would collide with the fragment-as-state design, and `frame-ancestors` is absent from the CSP because it's ignored in a `<meta>` tag (and the resulting console warning fails `pnpm smoke`) — it belongs on the server, which the lane deliberately ships header-free.",
      "isError": false
    }
